        "waited_before_the_first_take_s": 10.0,
        "why_the_wait": "This type glides to the placement its byte names instead of jumping to it, so a take struck at once reads where the image was passing. The wait is short of arrival at the furthest setting on purpose: the first take of each setting is the witness that says whether the glide was over, and the takes after it are the reading. The other 3D type carrying this byte does not glide and was not re-asked.",
        "loaded_once_per_setting": "The block was written and read back once per setting, not once per take, so the repeats say how well a take repeats rather than how well a write does."
